    <string name="privacy_section_1_title">1. Zero Cloud &amp; Zero Remote Tracking</string>
    <string name="privacy_section_1_desc">Ronova Mesh has zero server backend, zero telemetry, zero analytics, and zero third-party tracking. All communication is strictly peer-to-peer over local Bluetooth radios.</string>
    <string name="privacy_section_2_title">2. Military-Grade End-to-End Cryptography</string>
    <string name="privacy_section_2_desc">Every message is individually encrypted using ECDH secp256r1 key agreement with ephemeral AES-256-GCM. Intermediary relay nodes forward ciphertexts blindly without possessing the decryption keys.</string>
    <string name="privacy_section_3_title">3. Zero Location Tracking Guarantee</string>
    <string name="privacy_section_3_desc">Bluetooth permissions are strictly declared with \'neverForLocation\'. Ronova Mesh never accesses, queries, or logs GPS, cell tower, or Wi-Fi coordinates.</string>
    <string name="privacy_section_4_title">4. Real-time Ephemeral Audio Streaming</string>
    <string name="privacy_section_4_desc">Direct offline voice calls transmit real-time 16kHz PCM audio packets directly between paired nodes. Audio is never recorded, buffered to persistent storage, or monitored.</string>
    <string name="user_policy_sec_1_title">1. Decentralized Autonomous Network</string>
    <string name="user_policy_sec_1_desc">Ronova Mesh is an open decentralized mesh protocol. Users are solely responsible for verifying the authenticity of peer node fingerprints.</string>
    <string name="user_policy_sec_2_title">2. Voluntary Mesh Relaying</string>
    <string name="user_policy_sec_2_desc">Relaying messages for nearby community nodes extends network reach for everyone. You retain full control to enable or disable store-and-forward relaying at any time in Settings.</string>
    <string name="user_policy_sec_3_title">3. Emergency &amp; Off-Grid Readiness</string>
    <string name="user_policy_sec_3_desc">Ronova Mesh is engineered for natural disasters, remote expeditions, cellular blackouts, and communication emergencies where cellular networks are unavailable.</string>
